MID_SE_Tob_Oly_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_C_001: ♪On the goddess's back sprout the prettiest wings.\nWe mortal folk were born with no such things.♪
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_C_002: I wondered who was singing. Hello, Tobias.
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_C_003: Hm? Hey, it's Pia!
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_C_004: I am not Pia. I am Olympia!
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_C_005: C'mon, Pia, I know it's you.
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_C_006: Honestly, what is wrong with you? Oh, I see now.\nYou're thoroughly inebriated.
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_C_007: I cannot fathom how such a pretty melody came\nfrom such a crude man.
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_C_008: Hey, thanks! So you liked my song, huh?
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_C_009: Yes, it had a haunting sound that was resonant and\nsonorous...and rather melancholy.
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_C_010: I've never heard it before. Is it from Saramis?
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_C_011: Yeah. It's about the suffering and joy of our\nancestors, passed all the way down to us.
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_C_012: Hmm, fascinating. Would you mind teaching it\nto me?
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_C_013: Sure thing! The first verse goes like this...
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_C_014: ♪Gods are not men. And no, men are not gods.\nYet our hearts beat as one, against all the odds.♪
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_C_015: Well, how did I do? I am an excellent singer,\nyou must admit.
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_C_016: Yeah, you got some nice pipes. Still, though...\nsomething seemed off about it.
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_C_017: Wh-what?! Off? Me? Do please explain how\nMY voice was...off!
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_C_018: Sorry I can't nail it down for you. I'm not too good\nwith words.
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_C_019: What's missing is like... This'll sound cheesy, but the\nsoul of Saramis? I guess?
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_C_020: The soul? What am I supposed to do with such a\nvague critique?
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_C_021: Well, now that my singing has been disparaged,\nI have no choice. I must rise to the challenge.
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_C_022: I will show you that I can imbue that song of yours\nwith the soul of Saramis!
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_C_023: Hey, I like your spirit! Best of luck.
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_C_024: Oh, no, no, no. Let me be clear—YOU are going to\nteach me.
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_C_025: Huh?! You want my help? You're stranger than\nI thought.
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_C_026: You criticized my singing. Does it not seem obvious\nthat you should be the one to teach me?
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_C_027: Baw haw haw. Good one, lady! But sure, I'll teach\nyou. Just say the word.
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_B_001: Good day, Tobias. Thank you for the invitation.
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_B_002: Oh, good, you're here! C'mon, have a drink.
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_B_003: What? I thought you called me here to teach me\nabout the soul of Saramis.
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_B_004: You said that I must understand this soul if\nI wanted to sing that song of yours properly.
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_B_005: And that's what we're gonna do. It's why I got this\nparty set up!
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_B_006: Party? Surely you jest.
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_B_007: Dead serious. This is the only way.
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_B_008: Just drink up and have a chat, and the soul of\nSaramis will come to you naturally!
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_B_009: Is that really all it takes? Shouldn't we be studying\nthe history of the place or some such thing?
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_B_010: I wouldn't know where to start with that stuff.\nI'm no Bona.
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_B_011: The important thing is getting your feelings across.\nSinging's gotta be fun!
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_B_012: I suppose you have a point. In that case, I shall\njoin you.
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_B_013: Then we'll kick things off with some drinks!\nYou should have one too.
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_B_014: Eh, very well...
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_B_015: *sob* What a beautiful story!
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_B_016: There, there, it's OK! You're not drunk already,\nare you?
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_B_017: I am not! I'm simply moved by the plight of the\nSaramis people...and by Yu Phas's love!
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_B_018: The journey ahead is too harsh for her children, and\nso Yu Phas, in her kindness, walks alongside them...
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_B_019: What a dreadful fate! Waaah!
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_B_020: {SetColor=Gray}What am I gonna do? Never thought I'd be the one\ntaking care of a drunk.{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_B_021: I'm beginning to feel like I know Saramis! I want to\nhear more about it! You MUST tell me more!
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_B_022: Oh! We'll need more wine for that. Yes, bring some\nmore wine, pretty please!
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_B_023: Anything you say! Just wait right there.
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_B_024: That was a wonderful party. Thank you, Tobias!
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_B_025: Oh yeah? Well, long as you had a good time, Pia,\neverything's fine.
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_B_026: I think I finally understand the soul of the Saramis\npeople. I should be able to sing that song perfectly!
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_B_027: Oh yeah, that song you heard me singing. I forgot\nthat's what started all this.
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_B_028: It is. I'll be sure to sing for you again next\ntime, Tobias.
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_B_029: You sure? Sounds good...as long as it's not another\ndisaster of a party.
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_A_001: Thank you for waiting, Tobias. Today is the day!\nI will have you listen to me sing once again.
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_A_002: Today's the day, huh? Looking forward to it!
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_A_003: Listen well, and please appreciate how my studies\nhave improved my performance. Ahem, here I go...
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_A_004: ♪On the goddess's back sprout the prettiest wings.\nWe mortal folk were born with no such things.♪
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_A_005: Wow, Pia! That was way different than your last try.
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_A_006: I felt like I was right there in old Saramis, together\nwith the souls of the ancestors.
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_A_007: Haha! Of course you did. You cannot say my voice\nsounds "off" any longer!
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_A_008: I can't. That was good stuff. Guess that party\ndid the trick.
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_A_009: It certainly did. But that wasn't the only thing that\nhelped me succeed.
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_A_010: I have a longtime rival that I have never been able\nto surpass.
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_A_012: In my single-minded desire to beat her, I devoted\nmyself to perfecting my singing technique.
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_A_013: But singing is not just about technique. It's about\nfeeling emotions and transforming them into song.
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_A_014: You have reminded me of that. And so I thank you,\nTobias, from the bottom of my heart.
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_A_015: Hehe. Is that right? Glad I could help.
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_A_016: But y'know, this song is supposed to be sung over\nan instrument.
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_A_017: Usually, we use a traditional Saraminian drum called\na djemba.
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_A_018: Is that right? Can you play it for me?
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_A_019: I messed with it when I was younger. Don't really\nremember how anymore.
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_A_020: But hearing you sing makes me want to pick it\nup again!
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_A_021: Then by all means, please do! I would love to sing\nwhile you play the drum.
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_A_022: That's what I hoped to hear! It'll be great.
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_A_023: It sounds like a party is in order as well! We can\ninvite many guests and serve many drinks!
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_A_024: Errr— Let's go easy on the drinks, maybe.
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_A_025: What? Why? Since when have you ever believed\nin moderation?
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_A_026: That last party didn't go so great. You might wanna\nlay off the sauce, Pia.
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_A_027: I certainly do not...remember it...that way!\nIs that true?!
MID_SE_Tob_Oly_A_028: You didn't know? Damn, I'm really not too good\nwith words...